#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# discrete_asymptotic

#% text
# `discrete_asymptotic(f, k -> inf)` gives the leading asymptotic form of the sequence f(k) as the integer k grows.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# Factorials, gamma functions and binomials are first written by Stirling's formula `k! ~ sqrt(2 pi) k^(k + 1/2) exp(-k)`; the leading term is then that of `asymptotic`.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
discrete_asymptotic(factorial(k), k -> inf)
#% output
#= 2^(1/2)*exp(-k)*k^(1/2 + k)*pi^(1/2)

#% cell
discrete_asymptotic(binomial(2*k, k), k -> inf)
#% output
#= 2^(2*k)/(k^(1/2)*pi^(1/2))

#% cell
discrete_asymptotic((3*k^3 + 5)/(4*k^2 + 11), k -> inf)
#% output
#= (3/4)*k

#% cell
discrete_asymptotic((k^2 + 3*k)*2^k, k -> inf)
#% output
#= 2^k*k^2

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `asymptotic`, `discrete_limit`, `factorial`
